{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445150-adventure-era-ism-query","id":1445150,"title":"Adventure! Era -ism query","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-21T16:16:55-07:00","id":1445150,"title":"Adventure! Era -ism query","content":"I was going to post this in the TC Adventure! Kickstarter thread, but the topic is apparently closed for some reason.<br /> <br /> While reading the last of the Kickstarter backer manuscript previews, something bugged me about the Socialism entry in the Isms section, but it took me awhile to figure out exactly what. There are seven separate Ism subsections (Anti-Semitism, Classism, Fascism, Heterosexism/Homophobia, Racism, Sexism, and Socialism), but only six have lists of associated atrocities.<br /> <br /> The only vaguely bad thing said about socialism is that Mongolia had a &quot;violent uprising.&quot; Beyond that, we get phrases like, &quot;they sought the replacement of capitalism with something more equal and rational,&quot; &quot;socialism takes power away from the ruling class and distributes it evenly among the working class,&quot; and &quot;fueled by the belief in fairness and revolution, socialism spread among the working poor of Europe, especially among the peasants of Russia.&quot; If this is what socialism is supposed to mean, why is it in the <i>bad stuff</i> section?<br /> <br /> Given a few minutes of wikipedia research, I've come up with some Soviet specific <i>bad stuff</i> appropriate to the era. Anyone else have Soviet or non-Soviet examples of socialist atrocities before I submit my feedback on the issue through the kickstarter form?<br /> <br /> The Red Terror (1918): The Bolsheviks slaughtered their enemies. An estimated 100,000-200,000 died.<br /> <br /> The Gulags (1918-1960): The government agency in charge of the Soviet network of forced labor camps set up by order of Vladimir Lenin, reaching its peak during Joseph Stalin's rule from the 1930s to the early 1950s; recognized as a major instrument of political repression in the Soviet Union. The tentative consensus in contemporary Soviet historiography is that roughly 1,600,000 died due to detention in the camps.<br /> <br /> Dekulakization ()1929-1933): the Soviet campaign of political repressions, including arrests, deportations, or executions of millions of kulaks (prosperous peasants) and their families in the 1929\u20131932 period of the first five-year plan. To facilitate the expropriations of farmland, the Soviet government portrayed kulaks as class enemies of the USSR. There were 560,000 to 5 million estimated deaths.<br /> <br /> The Holodomor (1932-1933): The term Holodomor emphasises the famine's man-made and intentional aspects such as rejection of outside aid, confiscation of all household foodstuffs and restriction of population movement. Since 2006, the Holodomor has been recognized by Ukraine and 15 other countries as a genocide of the Ukrainian people carried out by the Soviet government. The death toll is estimated at 3-12 million.<br /> <br /> The Great Purge/Great Terror 1936-1938: It involved a large-scale repression of relatively wealthy peasants (kulaks); ethnic cleansing operations against ethnic minorities; a purge of the Communist Party, of government officials, and of the Red Army leadership; widespread police surveillance; suspicion of saboteurs; counter-revolutionaries; imprisonment; and arbitrary executions.Historians estimate the total number of deaths to be between 950,000 to 1.2 million.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T19:12:37-07:00","id":1445180,"title":"","content":"As I only just watched a series of LGBT+ history related documentaries, mainly on <i>Red / Lavender Scare</i> in 1950s in USA ( they were intertwined ), I can understand the scare of Socialism in American society. ( Even if it was rather exaggerated, conservative paranoia and panic. ) Staunched proposers of 'Scare' pointed the few of an examples you point to, @<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi\">Shepherdboi</a>.<br /> <br /> On the <b><i>Red / Lavender Scare</i></b> itself - Many people believe that being 'homosexual' ( LGBT+ in modern terms ) was sure sign you were Socialist - and by this, Communist. And Communists do not have place in USA government and society, after World War 2. As Socialism taken on the banners help of the oppressed people at the start of 20th century - not only lower class but Jews and some LGBT+ advocates also - all the <i>-Isms</i> were intertwined in society zeitgeist. And so, even middle Socialism became, de facto, nominative for Communism and all the horrors of that system, in America's minds eye.<br /> <br /> For inspiration on this subject - I can advise to see HBO documentary <a href=\"https://www.hbo.com/documentaries/bully-coward-victim-the-story-of-roy-cohn\" target=\"_blank\">B</a><a href=\"https://www.hbo.com/documentaries/bully-coward-victim-the-story-of-roy-cohn\" target=\"_blank\">ully. Coward. Victim. The Story of Roy Cohn</a> - chief counsel to Senator Joseph McCarthy. Cohn was born in 1927 and raised in exactly the political climate that <b>TC: Adventure!</b> 1930s are portraying. It reflects all the problems started in those times, in his life and later, mentality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-21-2021, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T19:29:41-07:00","id":1445183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445150-adventure-era-ism-query#post1445150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else have Soviet or non-Soviet examples of socialist atrocities before I submit my feedback on the issue through the kickstarter form?</div> </div> </div> </div>It involved atrocities on both sides, but the socialists in the Spanish Civil War (1936-1939) were definitely not squeaky clean. They had their own <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Terror_(Spain)\" target=\"_blank\">Red Terror</a> there which killed about 50,000 (A sizable portion of which were Catholic priests.) The <i>paseos</i> were particularly awful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"